      "message": "Now that it\u0027s much simpler, I realize we might be able to do a simplification.\n\nWould it work if we did the following :\n• Add a call to updateAppIdsTrafficPermission inside onUserAdded\n• Have this loop simply call onUserAdded with each user\n• Remove l.337, which is now useless\n\nI understand that we don\u0027t actually need to update traffic permissions when a user is added, but is it harmful ? Considering how rare it is, I don\u0027t think it\u0027s a problem if we do it.\n\nAlternatively you could also have a separate method called both from here and from onUserAdded. If you prefer we don\u0027t update traffic permissions in onUserAdded that method could have a boolean as an argument.\n\nWDYT ?",
